  "intro": {
    "language": "en",
    "text": "Mary Teresa Barra (née Makela; born December 24, 1961) is an American businesswoman who has been the chair and chief executive officer (CEO) of General Motors since January 15, 2014. She is the first female CEO of a 'Big Three' automaker. \nIn December 2013, GM named her to succeed Daniel Akerson as CEO. Before being named CEO, Barra was executive vice president of global product development, purchasing, and supply chain.\n\n",
    "sourceId": "wikipedia-en",
    "usage": "Research excerpt; paraphrase and cross-check before publication."
  },
